<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="skill">conductor-core</ansi> (blacksmithing recipe)

A forged core, wound tight in banded coils, built to carry a note the
way honest wire carries a current -- cleanly, completely, without losing
anything to the distance. Strike it and it does not ring so much as
wait, holding the sound until something asks it to let go. Smiths who
wind one speak of it like tuning rather than forging.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Crafting ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="yellow">Skill:</ansi>       blacksmithing (minimum 50)
  <ansi fg="yellow">Station:</ansi>     forge
  <ansi fg="yellow">Ingredients:</ansi> Silver Wire (x2), Steel Ingot (x1), Coal Dust (x1)

